{"t": 35.442, "n": 35, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I rewrote the triage note at `docs/tasks/i144.triage.md`. One gap is still open, so the route stays `discovery`.\n\n- **Review point:** CST-B8 still ends \"the entry stays\" with no exception, though CST-B17 lets `stats forget` remove an entry. I listed that as G7, a spec update, and did not mark it covered.\n- **Other links the reviewer flagged:**\n  - SIL-B1 defines `TEMPERGRAPH_LOOP=off|inline`, which TST-B8 relies on.\n  - LOS-B16 says `store prune` never prunes stats. `stats forget` is a different verb, so LOS-B16 stays true.\n- **Other gaps:** G1 to G6 are covered by existing behaviour and criterion pairs, which I read in the specs:\n  - G1: TST-B7 and TST-AC9.\n  - G2: TST-B8 and TST-AC10.\n  - G3: TST-B7 and TST-AC11.\n  - G4: CST-B17 and CST-AC6.\n  - G5: CST-B18 and CST-AC7.\n  - G6: CST-B19 and CST-AC9.\n- **Owner decisions:** None. The run has already returned to triage once, so it can't take `quick`.\n\nNot every gap is covered, because G7 isn't. I did not check the code or run any tests in this step.\n\nARTIFACT triage_note: docs/tasks/i144.triage.md\nARTIFACT gaps: some\nARTIFACT route: discovery\nARTIFACT covered: no", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "76339596-1b7a-4f8b-8265-8307f7562203"}
